From: OpenWiFi BCM4360 Project <bcm4360@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH 16/16] brcmfmac: pcie: BCM4360 test.316 R3b novram + console tail + P1-T mirror

Fire #9 (0015) dal dwa twarde fakty: (1) R3a -- strip "boardtype=" z NVRAM --
NIE poruszyla fw: wr_idx konsoli stoi na 0x27d (637), identyczny stall jak w
fire'ach #6-#8; (2) P1 -- PLAIN write MAILBOXINT (BAR0+0x48) := 0xFFFFFFFF
przed set_active -- readback 0x3 (zapis zamaskowany do 2 bitow doorbell), ale
PO set_active mbint=0: brcmf_chip_set_active CZYSCI mailbox, wiec zamrozone fw
nigdy nie widzialo doorbella. Kimptoc intstatus=0x300 (T284-era,
pre-set_active) pozostaje jedyna niewyjasniona obserwacja: to albo HW mirror
jego WLASNEGO pre-release zapisu, albo fw-side latch fw, ktore poszlo dalej
(1404 B konsoli). Trzy sondy 0016 rozstrzygaja to jednym fire'em #10:

a) bcm4360_test316=1 (master switch) -- R3b: w brcmf_pcie_download_fw_nvram,
   w miejscu zapisu NVRAM do TCM (bufor vars + token koncowy, ktory ladauje
   na TCM[ramsize-4]), CALA galaz zapisu jest POMIJANA: nie ma copy buforu
   vars, nie ma tokenu; write_ram32(ramsize-4, 0) zostawia marker sharedram
   na 0 -- dokladny substrat test.28 kimptoca, ktorego fw NIE mialo NVRAM
   (bmac_attach err 15 -> TRAP) i mimo to poszlo dalej niz 637 B. Kolejnosc
   guardow: test316 ma pierwszenstwo przed stripem 0015 (R3a) -- przy
   test316=1 bufor vars w ogole nie opuszcza RAM hosta, wiec strip (gdyby
   test315 tez byl ustawiony) jest bez znaczenia; snapshot test276
   varsz/vars16 czyta wtedy zera -- oczekiwane (i tak widzi fw: varsz=0).
   CPU-only, zero MMIO; bufor zwalniany niezapisany.

b) P1-T: warunek bloku P1 z 0015 (P3 read-only MAILBOXMASK + P1 PLAIN write
   MAILBOXINT := bcm4360_test315_db_val + readback, miedzy resetem
   INTERNAL_MEM a brcmf_chip_set_active, ARM w halt) rozszerzony o test316
   (bcm4360_test315 || bcm4360_test316); komunikaty pr_emerg uogolnione na
   "test.315/316". Bezposrednio PO readbacku P1 dwa pojedyncze windowed
   odczyty SB-side (BAR0+0x20 intstatus, BAR0+0x24 intmask) z bracketingiem
   + linia "P1-T mirror check: intstatus=... intmask=... mbint=...":
   intstatus=0x300 PRE-release (ARM w halt, nasz P1 wlasnie zlatchowal
   mbint=0x3) => kimptoc 0x300 = HW mirror jego wlasnego zapisu; ~0/0x80 =>
   brak mirroru -- kimptoc 0x300 = fw-side latch, jego fw poszlo past 637.

c) bcm4360_test316_console_tail=1 (NIEZALEZNY od test316 -- dziala przy
   test277=1): w bloku test.277 POST-POLL, zaraz po istniejacym wydruku
   naglowka (HEAD, pierwsze 128 B) konsoli -- odczyt OSTATNICH
   min(wr_idx, 96) bajtow bufora konsoli konczacych sie na wr_idx (guard:
   wr_idx < 96 -> od 0; wr_idx=0 -> skip z logiem). Mechanizm odczytu TCM
   identyczny z wydrukiem HEAD (brcmf_pcie_read_ram32 do chunka na stosie),
   start odczytu wyrownany do 4 B (<=3 B wczesniejszego tekstu konsoli z
   przodu; dlugosc wydruku konczy sie dokladnie na wr_idx), wydruk jako
   %*ph hex (<=64 B na linie, jedna linia kontynuacji) + jedna linia %*pE.
   Struktura niewazna (buf_addr poza TCM, wr_idx > buf_size -- walidacja w
   stylu test.278) -> skip z logiem. To zamyka najwieksza luke dowodowa:
   do tej pory znamy tylko NAGLOWEK bufora konsoli, ostatni wydruk fw
   przed stall jest kluczowy (nazwa funkcji, w ktorej fw utklo).

d) Zadnych innych zmian: T276/T277/T308/T309/T310/T311/T312/T313/T314/T315
   nietkniete (jedyny dotyk 0015: rozszerzenie warunku bloku P1 +
   uogolnienie komunikatow); DISCRIMINATOR 0015 zostaje gated na test315;
   gate 0012 i T309 nietkniete. Wszystkie parametry domyslnie 0 -> latka
   inerna.

Bezpieczenstwo (narzucone przez wedgi #4/#5): jedyne nowe operacje MMIO to
(b) dwa windowed odczyty BAR0 PRE-release z bracketingiem pr_emerg przed/po
(klasa T305 pre-release WRITE_LANDED + T315 DISCRIMINATOR, proven live w
#6-#9; stalling reads -- fire TYLKO z CTO 10-100 ms) i (c) petla <=25
odczytow TCM/BAR1 (brcmf_pcie_read_ram32) -- identyczna klasa co istniejacy
wydruk HEAD test.277 (32 odczyty, przetrwal kazdy fire #6-#9); ZERO nowych
zapisow MMIO. R3b to czysty CPU (host RAM, zero MMIO; bufor zwalniany).
Start odczytu TAIL wyrownany do 4 B (dol), wiec zadnych nie-wyrownanych
odczytow; dlugosc wydruku konczy sie na wr_idx. test316=0 i
test316_console_tail=0 (domyslnie) => zero roznicy kodowej i behawioralnej
(nowe parametry czytane wylacznie pod swoimi guardami). T309, gate 0012,
test313/test314 nietkniete (nic nie doklada w teardown).

Wymaga: test276=1 + test308=1 (pelny pipeline); test315 i test313 swiadomie
NIE ustawione w fire #10 (R3a obalone w #9; doorbell-anyway martwa sciezka);
bcm4360_test315_db_val=0xFFFFFFFF dalej steruje wartoscia zapisu P1(-T).
Fire tylko po setpci ASPM-off + CTO 10-100 ms na zywym urzadzeniu.

~160 lines, gated on chip 4360 + test316/test316_console_tail -- zero
behaviour change for every other chip and for the msgbuf path.

Signed-off-by: OpenWiFi BCM4360 Project <bcm4360@localhost>
---
 1 files changed, 157 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)
--- a/brcmfmac/pcie.c
+++ b/brcmfmac/pcie.c
@@ -280,6 +280,21 @@
 module_param(bcm4360_test315_no_master, uint, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(bcm4360_test315_no_master, "BCM4360 test.315 P4: skip pci_set_master() when 1 (chip 4360 only) -- bus-master/DMA control variable. kimptoc test.28 ran with bus mastering OFF and its fw went further than every brcmfmac port since (kimptoc-test28-comparison.md sec.4-H3); the olmsg transport does not work yet either way, so DMA is not lost. The readback is the test.315 discriminator. Requires bcm4360_test315=1. (1=skip set_master, 0=default)");
 
+/* test.316: R3b -- NVRAM download skip (no vars buffer, no end token at
+ * TCM[ramsize-4]). With test316=1 the vars buffer never leaves host RAM, so
+ * it takes PRECEDENCE over the test.315 R3a strip (a strip, if test315 is
+ * set too, is moot). Also the size of the test.316 console TAIL window
+ * (the independent console-tail param, see its MODULE_PARM_DESC). */
+#define BCM4360_T316_CONSOLE_TAIL_BYTES	96
+
+static uint bcm4360_test316;
+module_param(bcm4360_test316, uint, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(bcm4360_test316, "BCM4360 test.316 master switch (fire #10; fire #9 verdict: R3a did NOT move the fw -- console wr_idx stayed 0x27d=637, and the P1 pre-release doorbell read back 0x3 while post-set_active mbint=0 => brcmf_chip_set_active CLEARS the mailbox, the frozen fw never saw the doorbell). (a) R3b NVRAM: SKIP the whole NVRAM download in brcmf_pcie_download_fw_nvram -- no vars buffer copy, no end token at TCM[ramsize-4] (the write_ram32(ramsize-4, 0) above leaves the sharedram marker at 0, exactly the no-NVRAM state): the exact kimptoc test.28 substrate, whose fw had NO NVRAM (bmac_attach err 15 -> TRAP) and still ran past 637 console bytes. Takes PRECEDENCE over the test.315 R3a strip (with test316=1 the buffer never leaves host RAM, so a strip is moot); the test276 varsz/vars16 snapshot then reads zeros -- expected, and the fw sees the same (varsz=0). CPU-only, zero MMIO. (b) P1-T: the 0015 pre-release block (P3 MAILBOXMASK read + P1 PLAIN write MAILBOXINT BAR0+0x48 := bcm4360_test315_db_val + readback, between the INTERNAL_MEM reset and brcmf_chip_set_active, ARM still halted) ALSO runs under test316=1 (condition bcm4360_test315 || bcm4360_test316; db_val default 0xFFFFFFFF), and immediately after the P1 readback two windowed SB-side reads complete the P1-T mirror check: SB intstatus (BAR0+0x20) and SB intmask (BAR0+0x24) PRE-release -- intstatus=0x300 there => kimptoc's 0x300 was a HW mirror of his own pre-release write; ~0/0x80 => no mirror (kimptoc's 0x300 = fw-side latch, his fw ran past 637). Everything else untouched: T276/T277/T308/T309/T310/T311/T312/T313/T314/T315 semantics unchanged, the test.312 gate and the T309 hold stay as they are, the 0015 post-set_active DISCRIMINATOR stays gated on test315 only. Requires test276=1 + test308=1; fire only with ASPM off + CTO 10-100 ms. (1=enable, 0=off)");
+
+static uint bcm4360_test316_console_tail;
+module_param(bcm4360_test316_console_tail, uint, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(bcm4360_test316_console_tail, "BCM4360 test.316 console TAIL (INDEPENDENT of bcm4360_test316 -- runs whenever the test.277 POST-POLL console dump runs, i.e. with test277=1): after the existing first-128-B HEAD dump, read the LAST min(wr_idx, 96) bytes of the fw console buffer ending at wr_idx -- only the HEAD of the console is known so far and the last fw print before the stall is the key evidence (wr_idx=0x27d=637 in fires #6-#9). Same TCM dword-read mechanism as the HEAD dump (brcmf_pcie_read_ram32 into a stack chunk), read from the 4 B aligned start (<=3 B of earlier console text in front; the printed span ends exactly at wr_idx), printed as %*ph hex (<=64 B per line, one continuation line) + one %*pE ASCII-escaped line. Skipped with a log line when wr_idx=0 or the struct fails validation (buf_addr in TCM, wr_idx <= buf_size, test.278-style). (1=enable, 0=off)");
+
 static int bcm4360_test308_olmsg_cdc;
 module_param(bcm4360_test308_olmsg_cdc, int, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(bcm4360_test308_olmsg_cdc, "BCM4360 test.308: PCI-CDC (olmsg) transport, phase 1+2. Phase 1: replace the msgbuf sharedram-ptr handshake poll (TCM[ramsize-4], guaranteed -ENODEV on this fw) with a best-effort si[+0x2028] poll (10 ms x 200, then CONTINUE), skip msgbuf shared-struct/ring setup, proto_type=BCDC. Phase 2: txctl/rxctl over the olmsg ring (T276 DMA buffer -- requires bcm4360_test276_shared_info=1), D2H drain in the threaded ISR on BAR0+0x48 bit 8, per-cycle mask BAR0+0x4C |= 0x100. txdata stays a stub until phase 3. Gated: only for chip 4360; all other chips keep the msgbuf path. (1=enable, 0=off)");
@@ -1734,21 +1749,25 @@
  * when the machine dies on that op); the pre-release BAR0 read/write
  * class is proven on the live device in experiment #1 fire 2 (T305
  * pre-release MAILBOXMASK write + readback, WRITE_LANDED) and by every
- * later windowed single (fires #6/#7). */
